course: dictionary
lesson: 9019
title: A seabird called the skua
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about nature, and you can work out their meaning from the sentence and the words around them. «Snowy owls, Arctic foxes, stoats and skuas depend on lemmings.» The animals in this list all need lemmings to live, so a skua must be an animal too.
explain: The dictionary tells us more: a skua is a large brown seabird that lives in cold northern and southern seas. Context and the dictionary work well together. First use the sentence to guess, then check your guess in the dictionary.
explain: Words also tell a story. «Visitors to Scottish islands are warned that great skuas dive at people near their nests.» Dive and warned show that skuas can be dangerous to people who come too close. Local people in Shetland call them «bonxies», which is a name you will only hear there.
fact: A skua is a large brown seabird.
fact: Skuas live in cold northern and southern seas.
fact: «Kleptoparasitism» means stealing food from another animal.
fact: Skuas often chase other seabirds until they drop or bring up their food.
fact: Skuas attack people who come near their nests, so visitors to Shetland are warned about them.
exercise: «Snowy owls, Arctic foxes, stoats and skuas depend on lemmings.» What kind of thing is a skua? | A place | A rock | *An animal | A kind of food
exercise: Visitors to Shetland are warned that great skuas dive at people near their nests. What does this tell you about skuas? | They only eat grass | They are friendly and like visitors | They live in shops | *They can attack people who come too close to their nests
exercise: Skuas chase other seabirds until the seabirds drop their food. What is this way of feeding called? | Fishing with nets | Sleeping in the sun | Growing seeds | *Kleptoparasitism, which means stealing food
test:  Local people in Shetland call great skuas «bonxies». What is a bonxie? | A Shetland sheep | A kind of boat | A type of fish | *A great skua
test:  A skua chases a gull until the gull drops its fish. What is the skua doing? | *Stealing food from another bird | Building a nest | Sleeping on the sea | Feeding its chicks grass
exam:  Where do skuas live? | In hot deserts | *In cold northern and southern seas | In deep caves | In warm forests
